              "uco-observable:stringValue": "Query Reports Utilities Help Log Out\n\nBradyAd,DEFWVR\n\nU.S. District Court\nUnited States District Court for the District of Alaska (Anchorage)\nCRIMINAL DOCKET FOR CASE #: 3:24-cr-00091-SLG-KFR All Defendants\n\nCase title: USA v. Herrera Date Filed: 08/22/2024\n\nAssigned to: Sharon L. Gleason\nReferred to: Kyle F. Reardon\n\nDefendant (1)\nSeth Herrera represented by Ben W. Muse\nFederal Public Defender Office\n188 W. Northern Lights Blvd.\nSte 700\nAnchorage, AK 99503\n907-646-3407\nEmail: benjamin_muse@fd.org\nLEAD ATTORNEY\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: Federal Public Defender\n\nPending Counts Disposition\n18:2252A(a)(1),(b)(1) TRANSPORTATION OF CHILD PORNOGRAPHY\n(1)\n18:2252A(a)(2),(b)(1) RECEIPT OF CHILD PORNOGRAPHY\n(2)\n18:2252A(a)(5)(b),(b)(2) POSSESSION OF CHILD PORNOGRAPHY\n(3)\n\nHighest Offense Level (Opening)\nFelony\n\nTerminated Counts Disposition\nNone\n\nHighest Offense Level (Terminated)\nNone\n\nComplaints Disposition\nNone\n\nPlaintiff\nUSA represented by Mac Caille Petursson\nDOJ-USAO\n222 W 7th Ave\nAnchorage, AK 99501\n907-271-2175\nEmail: mac.caille.petursson@usdoj.gov\nLEAD ATTORNEY\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: Assistant US Attorney\n\nRachel Lieber Rothberg\nDOJ-Crm\n1301 New York Ave NW\n11th Fl.\nWashington, DC 20530\n202-603-9145\nEmail: rachel.rothberg@usdoj.gov\nLEAD ATTORNEY\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: Assistant US Attorney\n\nDate Filed # Docket Text\n08/22/2024 1 INDICTMENT COVER SHEET(S) AND SIGNATURES as to Seth Herrera (1) count(s) 1, 2, 3. (Attachments: # 1 Criminal Cover Sheet re Defendant Herrera) (BJK, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 08/23/2024)\n08/22/2024 2 INDICTMENT as to Seth Herrera. (BJK, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 08/23/2024)\n08/23/2024 Notice of Arrest of Seth Herrera. Defendant arrested 8/23/24 and is located at ACCE. (BJK, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 08/23/2024)\n08/23/2024 3 KFR TEXT ORDER Setting Hearing as to Seth Herrera: Arraignment on Indictment/Detention Hearing set for 8/27/2024 at 1:30 PM in Anchorage Courtroom 6 before Kyle F. Reardon. (BJK, COURT STAFF)\n(Entered: 08/23/2024)\n08/23/2024 4 MEMORANDUM DETENTION by USA as to Seth Herrera (Petursson, Mac Caille) (Entered: 08/23/2024)\n08/23/2024 5 NOTICE OF ATTORNEY APPEARANCE: Ben W. Muse appearing for Seth Herrera (Muse, Ben) (Entered: 08/23/2024)\n08/27/2024 6 Arrest Warrant Returned Executed on 8/23/24 in case as to Seth Herrera. (PXS, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 08/27/2024)\n08/27/2024 7 PRETRIAL SERVICES REPORT (Sealed) as to Seth Herrera. (Edwards, Cassidy) (Entered: 08/27/2024)\n08/27/2024 8 MINUTE ENTRY for proceedings held before Judge Kyle F. Reardon: Arraignment on Indictment 2 /Detention Hearing as to Seth Herrera held 1:41 PM to 2:09 PM on 08/27/2024 and recorded in Anchorage Courtroom\n6. Copy of the Indictment 2 given to defendant. Defendant waived full reading; summarized. Defendant advised of general rights, charges, and penalties. Ben W. Muse, FPD appointed. FPD notified. Plea entered not\nguilty to Counts 1, 2 and 3 of the Indictment 2 and DENIED the criminal forfeiture allegation. Right to Speedy Trial Act Waiver FILED. Court and counsel heard re Defendant's decision not to sign the Defendant's\nWaiver of all Presence at this time. Discovery due 09/20/2024. Discovery Management Conference set for 10/01/2024 at 1:30 PM in Anchorage Courtroom 6 before Kyle F. Reardon. Trial Scheduling Conference to be set\nand separate order to issue. Court found excludable delay under 18 USC section 3161(h)(7)(A) Continuance granted per the ends of justice will be served by granting this continuance and outweigh the best interest of the\npublic and the defendant in a speedy trial; (h)(7)(B)(i) failure to continue would stop further proceedings or result in miscarriage of justice; and (h)(7)(B)(iv) in order to obtain counsel, substitute counsel, or give\nreasonable time to prepare from 08/27/2024 through 10/01/2024.\n\nUnder Criminal Rule 5(f), the government is ordered to comply with its disclosure obligations under Brady v. Maryland and related cases. Failure to do so may result in sanctions. This order incorporates the provisions of\nMGO 21-11 and a written order is attached.\n\nCourt and counsel heard re Defendant's Oral Motion for Release with Conditions. Arguments heard. Court and counsel heard re government's exhibits taken from the defendant's cell phones shown to the court and Ms.\nStaft.Defendant's Oral Motion for Release with Conditions DENIED. Court ordered defendant's detention. APPEARANCES: Defendant present, In-custody; Rachel Lieber Rothberg & Mac Caille Petursson, AUSA;\nGretchen L. Staft for Ben W. Muse, FPD; Cassidy Williams, USPO. (DXB, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 08/28/2024)\n08/27/2024 9 CJA 23 Financial Affidavit by Seth Herrera. (DXB, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 08/28/2024)\n08/27/2024 10 ORDER OF DETENTION as to Seth Herrera. Signed by Judge Kyle F. Reardon on 08/27/2024. (DXB, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 08/28/2024)\n09/05/2024 11 SLG TEXT ORDER as to Seth Herrera: A Trial Scheduling Conference is scheduled for October 29, 2024, at 1:00 p.m. in Anchorage Courtroom 2. (JDS, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 09/05/2024)\n09/12/2024 12 MOTION for Protective Order Regarding Discovery (Unopposed) by USA as to Seth Herrera. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Order)(Petursson, Mac Caille) (Entered: 09/12/2024)\n09/17/2024 13 ORDER GRANTING Motion for Protective Order Regarding Discovery (Unopposed) 12 as to Seth Herrera. Signed by Judge Kyle F. Reardon on 9/16/2024. (ELH, CHAMBERS STAFF) (Entered: 09/17/2024)\n10/01/2024 14 MINUTE ENTRY for proceedings held before Judge Kyle F. Reardon:Discovery Management Conference as to Seth Herrera held 1:39 PM to 1:44 PM on 10/1/2024 and recorded in Anchorage Courtroom 6. Court and\ncounsel heard re status of case and discovery. Outstanding discovery due 10/15/2024. APPEARANCES: Defendant present, in-custody; Rachel Lieber Rothberg and MacCaille Petursson, AUSAs; Ben W. Muse, FPD.\n(ASH, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 10/02/2024)\n10/02/2024 15 DISCOVERY MANAGEMENT CONFERENCE ORDER as to Seth Herrera. Signed by Judge Kyle F. Reardon on 10/1/2024. (ELH, CHAMBERS STAFF) (Entered: 10/02/2024)\n10/04/2024 16 UNOPPOSED MOTION to Appear Telephonically by USA as to Seth Herrera. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Order)(Rothberg, Rachel) (Entered: 10/04/2024)\n10/07/2024 17 RIGHT TO SPEEDY TRIAL ACT/FSA ACKNOWLEDGMENT & WAIVER Trial by Seth Herrera. (Muse, Ben) (Entered: 10/07/2024)\n10/07/2024 18 NOTICE of filing: Defendant's Waiver of ALL Presence - In Person and Remote by Seth Herrera (Muse, Ben) (Entered: 10/07/2024)\n10/11/2024 19 SLG TEXT ORDER: The United States' Unopposed Motion to Appear Telephonically at Docket 16 is GRANTED. Counsel may appear telephonically at the October 29, 2024 trial scheduling conference by dialing 571-\n353-2301 (Call ID 020262828, PIN 487051) approximately five minutes before the scheduled conference time. (JDS, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 10/11/2024)\n10/15/2024 20 SLG TEXT ORDER as to Seth Herrera: Due to a conflict in the Court's calendar the time of the Trial Scheduling Conference on October 29, 2024, is amended to the same day at 12:45 p.m. in Anchorage Courtroom 2.\n(SCD, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 10/15/2024)\n10/28/2024 21 SLG TEXT ORDER as to Seth Herrera: Due to a conflict in the Court's calendar, the Trial Scheduling Conference on October 29, 2024, is VACATED and rescheduled to October 31, 2024, at 12:00 p.m. in Anchorage\nCourtroom 1. (SCD, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 10/28/2024)\n10/31/2024 22 MINUTE ENTRY for proceedings held before Judge Sharon L. Gleason: Status Conference (Trial Scheduling Conference) as to Seth Herrera held 11:58 a.m. to 12:02 p.m. on 10/31/2024 and recorded in Anchorage\nCourtroom 1. Defendant waived appearance. Court and counsel heard re defendant's unopposed oral motion for a status hearing in January and setting motions deadline GRANTED. Status Conference set for 1/22/2025 at\n1:30 PM in Anchorage Courtroom 2 before Sharon L. Gleason. Motions deadline due by 12/16/2024; Response due by 12/30/2024.\n\nThe court found the ends of justice served by taking such action outweigh the best interest of the public and the defendant in a speedy trial and excluded time under 18:3161 (h)(7)(A);(h)(7)(B) (i) and (iv) until 1/22/2025.\nAPPEARANCES: Defendant not present, In-Custody (waived); Mac Caille Petursson, AUSA; Rachel Lieber Rothberg, AUSA (tel); Ben W. Muse, FPD. (IAH, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 10/31/2024)\n01/10/2025 23 UNOPPOSED MOTION to Continue Status Hearing by Seth Herrera. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Order)(Muse, Ben) (Entered: 01/10/2025)\n01/14/2025 24 SLG TEXT ORDER: The Unopposed Motion to Continue Status Conference at Docket 23 is GRANTED. The Status Conference on January 22, 2025 at 1:30 p.m. is VACATED and rescheduled to February 13, 2025 at\n9:45 a.m. in Anchorage Courtroom 2. The Court finds the ends of justice served by taking such action outweigh the best interest of the public and the defendant in a speedy trial and excludes time under 18 U.S.C. \u00a7 3161\n(h)(7)(A); (h)(7)(B)(i); (h)(7)(B)(iv) until 2/13/2025. (JDS, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 01/14/2025)\n01/29/2025 25 UNOPPOSED MOTION to Appear Telephonically by USA as to Seth Herrera. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Order)(Rothberg, Rachel) (Entered: 01/29/2025)\n02/04/2025 26 SLG TEXT ORDER: The Motion to Appear Telephonically at Docket 25 is GRANTED. Counsel may appear telephonically for the February 13, 2025 Status Conference by dialing 571-353-2301 (Call ID 020262828,\nPin 487051) approximately five minutes before the scheduled hearing time. (CFR, CHAMBERS STAFF) (Entered: 02/04/2025)\n02/13/2025 27 MINUTE ENTRY for proceedings held before Judge Sharon L. Gleason: Status Conference as to Seth Herrera held 9:47 AM to 9:50 AM on 2/13/2025. Court and counsel heard re ongoing plea negotiations, trial\nscheduling, and estimated length of trial 2 days. Dispositive Motions due by 3/28/2025. Final Pretrial Conference set for 6/11/2025 at 2:30 PM and Trial by Jury set for 6/23/2025 at 8:30 AM in Anchorage Courtroom 2\nbefore Judge Sharon L. Gleason. Trial scheduling order to issue. The court found the ends of justice served by taking such action and outweigh the best interest of the public and the defendant in a speedy trial and\nexcluded time under 18 U.S.C. \u00a7\u00a7 3161 (h)(7)(A); (h)(7)(B)(i); and (h)(7)(B)(iv) from 2/13/2025 through 6/23/2025. APPEARANCES: Defendant WAIVED, in-custody; Rachel Lieber Rothberg, AUSA (TEL); Burke\nWonnell for Ben W. Muse, FPD; Sonja L. Reeves, Official Court Reporter. (JDS, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 02/13/2025)\n02/13/2025 28 CRIMINAL PRETRIAL AND TRIAL SCHEDULING ORDER as to Seth Herrera: Dispositive Motions due by 3/28/2025. Final Pretrial Conference set for 6/11/2025 at 2:30 PM and Trial by Jury set for 6/23/2025 at\n8:30 AM in Anchorage Courtroom 2. See Order for additional deadlines. Signed by Judge Sharon L. Gleason on 2/13/2025. (JDS, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 02/13/2025)\n03/07/2025 29 NOTICE OF INTENT TO CHANGE PLEA as to Seth Herrera (Muse, Ben) (Entered: 03/07/2025)\n03/11/2025 30 SLG TEXT ORDER as to Seth Herrera: In light of the Notice of Intent to Change Plea at Docket 29 , the Final Pretrial Conference set for June 11, 2025 and Trial by Jury set for June 23, 2025 are VACATED. This matter\nis referred to Magistrate Judge Kyle F. Reardon for a change of plea hearing. (JDS, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 03/11/2025)\n03/11/2025 31 KFR TEXT ORDER SETTING HEARING as to Seth Herrera: Proposed Change of Plea Hearing set for 3/19/2025 at 1:30 PM in Anchorage Courtroom 6 before Judge Kyle F. Reardon. The parties are directed to file\nthe signed plea agreement, or provide an unsigned courtesy copy to the Court, no later than Noon on the day prior to the proposed change of plea hearing (see Local Criminal Rule 11.2(a)). If no plea agreement was\nreached, the parties are to file a Notice of Stipulated Facts. (ELH, CHAMBERS STAFF) (Entered: 03/11/2025)\n03/18/2025 32 MOTION to Vacate Proposed Change of Plea Hearing (NON-OPPOSED) by Seth Herrera. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Order)(Muse, Ben) (Entered: 03/18/2025)\n03/18/2025 33 MOTION to Expedite Consideration re 32 by Seth Herrera. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Order)(Muse, Ben) (Entered: 03/18/2025)\n03/18/2025 34 MOTION for Hearing re Status by Seth Herrera. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Order)(Muse, Ben) (Entered: 03/18/2025)\n03/18/2025 35 KFR TEXT ORDER GRANTING 33 Motion for Expedited Consideration as to Seth Herrera. (ELH, CHAMBERS STAFF) (Entered: 03/18/2025)\n03/18/2025 36 KFR TEXT ORDER as to as to Seth Herrera: After due consideration, Mr. Herrera's Non-Opposed Motion to Vacate Proposed Change of Plea hearing 32 , the motion is GRANTED. IT IS ORDERED that the Proposed\nChange of Plea Hearing set for March 19, 2025, at 1:30 p.m. is VACATED. (ELH, CHAMBERS STAFF) (Entered: 03/18/2025)\n03/21/2025 37 SLG TEXT ORDER as to Seth Herrera: The Non-Opposed Motion to Schedule Status Conference at Docket 34 is GRANTED. A Status Conference is scheduled for March 31, 2025, at 2:00 p.m. before District Judge\nSharon L. Gleason in Anchorage Courtroom 2. (JDS, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 03/21/2025)\n03/24/2025 38 UNOPPOSED MOTION to Appear Telephonically by USA as to Seth Herrera. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Order)(Rothberg, Rachel) (Entered: 03/24/2025)\n03/26/2025 40 SLG TEXT ORDER: The Unopposed Motion to Appear Telephonically at Docket 38 is GRANTED. Ms. Rothberg may appear telephonically by at the Status Conference on March 31, 2025 at 2:00 p.m. by dialing 571-\n353-2301 (Call ID 020262828, Pin 487051) approximately five minutes before the scheduled hearing time. (JDS, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 03/26/2025)\n03/27/2025 41 MOTION NON-OPPOSED Defense Counsel's Telephonic Appearance re 37 Order,, Terminate Motions,, Set Hearings, by Seth Herrera. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Order)(Muse, Ben) (Entered: 03/27/2025)\n03/27/2025 42 MOTION to Expedite Consideration re 41 by Seth Herrera. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Order)(Muse, Ben) (Entered: 03/27/2025)\n03/27/2025 43 SLG TEXT ORDER: Defendant's Unopposed Motion for Telephonic Appearance at Docket 41 and Motion to Expedite at Docket 42 are each GRANTED. Attorney Ben W. Muse may participate telephonically in the\nStatus Conference set for March 31, 2025, at 2:00 p.m. by dialing 571-353-2301 (Call ID 020262828, Pin 487051) approximately five minutes before the scheduled hearing time. (JDS, COURT STAFF) (Entered:\n03/27/2025)\n03/31/2025 44 MINUTE ENTRY for proceedings held before Judge Sharon L. Gleason: Trial Scheduling Conference (Status Conference) as to Seth Herrera held 2:00 p.m. to 2:09 p.m. on 3/31/2025. Court and counsel heard re setting\ntrial date in June or later, estimated trial length of 2 days for the government, and setting standard motions deadline. Final Pretrial Conference is set for 7/17/2025 at 2:00 p.m. and Trial by Jury set for 8/6/2025 at 8:30\na.m. in Anchorage Courtroom 2 before Judge Sharon L. Gleason. Trial scheduling order to issue. The court found the ends of justice served by taking such action and outweigh the best interest of the public and the\ndefendant in a speedy trial and excluded time under 18 U.S.C. \u00a7\u00a7 3161 (h)(7)(A); (h)(7)(B)(i); and (h)(7)(B)(iv) from 3/31/2025 through 8/6/2025. APPEARANCES: Defendant WAIVED, in-custody; Rachel Lieber\nRotherberg, AUSA (telephonic); Ben W. Muse, FPD (telephonic); Stacy M. Baldwin, Official Court Reporter. (ANM, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 04/01/2025)\n04/02/2025 45 AMENDED CRIMINAL PRETRIAL AND TRIAL SCHEDULING ORDER as to Seth Herrera: See order for details. Signed by Judge Sharon L. Gleason on 4/1/2025. (SCD, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 04/02/2025)\n05/12/2025 46 NOTICE of Expert Witness Under Federal Rule 16(a)(1)(G) by USA as to Seth Herrera (Rothberg, Rachel) (Entered: 05/12/2025)\n05/12/2025 47 MOTION for Extension of Time to File Pretrial Motions (NON-OPPOSED & EXPEDITED CONSIDERATION) by Seth Herrera. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Order)(Muse, Ben) (Entered: 05/12/2025)\n05/13/2025 48 SLG TEXT ORDER as to Seth Herrera: Defendant's Non-Opposed Expedited Motion to Extend Deadline to File Pretrial Motions is GRANTED. The deadline to file dispositive motions is extended to May 19, 2025.\n(JDS, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 05/13/2025)\n05/16/2025 49 NOTICE regarding Parallel Proceedings by USA as to Seth Herrera (Rothberg, Rachel) (Entered: 05/16/2025)\n05/21/2025 50 MOTION for Extension of Time to File Pretrial Motions (NON-OPPOSED & EXPEDITED CONSIDERATION) by Seth Herrera. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Order)(Muse, Ben) (Entered: 05/21/2025)\n05/22/2025 51 SLG TEXT ORDER as to Seth Herrera: Defendant's Non-Opposed Expedited Motion to Extend Deadline to File Pretrial Motions at Docket 50 is GRANTED. The deadline to file dispositive motions is extended to May\n30, 2025. (JDS, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 05/22/2025)\n05/30/2025 52 MOTION for Extension of Time to File Pretrial Motions (NON-OPPOSED & EXPEDITED CONSIDERATION) by Seth Herrera. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Order)(Muse, Ben) (Entered: 05/30/2025)\n05/30/2025 53 SLG TEXT ORDER as to Seth Herrera: The Non-Opposed Expedited Motion to Extend Deadline to File Pretrial Motions at Docket 52 is GRANTED. The deadline for pretrial motions is extended to June 6, 2025. (JDS,\nCOURT STAFF) (Entered: 05/30/2025)\n06/11/2025 54 MOTION to Suppress Evidence by Seth Herrera. (Attachments: # 1 Exhibit D-1 Warrants, # 2 Exhibit D-2 Law Enforcement Video, # 3 Exhibit D-3 Transcript re Law Enforcement Video, # 4 Exhibit D-4 CID Report\n5/8/2024, # 5 Exhibit D-5 Search Warrants Execution, # 6 Exhibit D-6 CID Report 5/7/2024, # 7 Exhibit D-7 CID Report 5/14/2024, # 8 Exhibit D-8 Seized Property List SA Elizter, # 9 Proposed Order)(Muse, Ben)\n(Entered: 06/11/2025)\n06/11/2025 55 MOTION To Accept Late Filing re 54 MOTION to Suppress Evidence by Seth Herrera. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Order)(Muse, Ben) (Entered: 06/11/2025)\n06/12/2025 56 UNOPPOSED MOTION for Extension of Time to File Response/Reply (on EXPEDITED CONSIDERATION) by USA as to Seth Herrera. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Order)(Rothberg, Rachel) (Entered: 06/12/2025)\n06/12/2025 57 MOTION re 56 UNOPPOSED MOTION for Extension of Time to File Response/Reply (on EXPEDITED CONSIDERATION) Motion for Expedited Consideration by USA as to Seth Herrera. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed\nOrder)(Rothberg, Rachel) (Entered: 06/12/2025)\n06/12/2025 58 MOTION to Seal 54 Unopposed by Seth Herrera. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Order)(Muse, Ben) (Entered: 06/12/2025)\n06/12/2025 59 MOTION to File Exhibits Under Seal Pursuant to Protective Order re 54 MOTION to Suppress Evidence (Unopposed) by Seth Herrera. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Order)(Muse, Ben) (Entered: 06/12/2025)\n06/12/2025 60 SLG TEXT ORDER as to Seth Herrera: Defendant's Expedited Motion to Accept Late Filing at Docket 55 is GRANTED. Defendant's Motion to Suppress at Docket 54 is accepted as filed. The Government's Motion for\nExpedited Consideration at Docket 57 and Unopposed Motion for Extension of Time to File Response to Motion to Suppress at Docket 56 are each GRANTED. The Government shall file a response to Defendant's\nMotion to Suppress no later than July 18, 2025. (JDS, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 06/12/2025)\n06/16/2025 61 MOTION to Continue Trial (UNOPPOSED) by Seth Herrera. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Order)(Muse, Ben) (Entered: 06/16/2025)\n06/16/2025 62 SLG TEXT ORDER as to Seth Herrera: The Unopposed Motion to Seal Defendant's Motion to Suppress at Docket 58 is GRANTED. The motion at Docket 54 shall be sealed. Counsel for defendant shall file a redacted\nversion of the Motion to Suppress as soon as practicable. (JDS, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 06/16/2025)\n06/16/2025 63 SLG TEXT ORDER as to Seth Herrera: The Unopposed Motion to File Exhibits Under Seal Pursuant to Protective Order at Docket 59 is GRANTED. Defense counsel is permitted to file Exhibits D-1 through D-8 under\nseal in support of the motion at Docket 54. (JDS, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 06/16/2025)\n06/17/2025 64 REDACTION by Seth Herrera to 54 MOTION to Suppress Evidence filed by Seth Herrera (Attachments: # 1 Motion to Suppress Evidence)(Muse, Ben) (Entered: 06/17/2025)\n06/17/2025 65 SEALED NOTICE Exhibits Under Seal Authorized by the Court at Docket No. 63 by Seth Herrera re 54 MOTION to Suppress Evidence (Attachments: # 1 Exhibit D-1, # 2 Exhibit D-3, # 3 Exhibit D-4, # 4 Exhibit D-5,\n# 5 Exhibit D-6, # 6 Exhibit D-7, # 7 Exhibit D-8)(Muse, Ben) (Entered: 06/17/2025)\n06/17/2025 66 NOTICE of Filing Exhibit Conventionally and Under Seal by Seth Herrera re 54 MOTION to Suppress Evidence (Muse, Ben) (Entered: 06/17/2025)\n06/18/2025 67 SLG TEXT ORDER as to Seth Herrera: Mr. Herrera's Unopposed Motion to Continue Trial at Docket 61 is GRANTED. The Trial by Jury scheduled for August 6, 2025, Final Pretrial Conference scheduled for July 17,\n2025, and all remaining pretrial deadlines are VACATED. A status hearing is set for August 6, 2025 at 10:00 a.m. in Anchorage Courtroom 2. The Court finds excludable delay through 8/6/2025 under 18 U.S.C. \u00a7\u00a7 3161\n(h)(7)(A); (h)(7)(B)(i) and (iv) as the ends of justice served by taking such action outweigh the best interest of the public and the defendant in a speedy trial. (RMC, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 06/18/2025)\n06/23/2025 68 UNOPPOSED MOTION to Appear Telephonically by USA as to Seth Herrera. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Order)(Rothberg, Rachel) (Entered: 06/23/2025)\n06/24/2025 69 SLG TEXT ORDER: The Unopposed Motion to Appear Telephonically at Docket 68 is GRANTED. Attorney Rachel Rothberg may participate telephonically in the Status Conference set for August 6, 2025 at 10:00 a.m.\nby dialing 571-353-2301 (Call ID 020262828, PIN 487051) approximately five minutes before the scheduled conference time. (JDS, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 06/24/2025)\n07/18/2025 70 RESPONSE in Opposition by USA as to Seth Herrera re 54 MOTION to Suppress Evidence (Attachments: # 1 Exhibit 1)(Rothberg, Rachel) (Entered: 07/18/2025)\n07/18/2025 71 MOTION to Accept Overlength Brief re 70 Response in Opposition by USA as to Seth Herrera. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Order)(Rothberg, Rachel) (Entered: 07/18/2025)\n07/18/2025 72 SEALED NOTICE of Filing Sealed Exhibit by USA as to Seth Herrera (Attachments: # 1 Exhibit 1)(Rothberg, Rachel) (Entered: 07/18/2025)\n07/23/2025 74 MOTION for Leave to File Reply by Seth Herrera. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Order)(Muse, Ben) Modified on 7/25/2025 to create relationship to dkt 72, 54. (RMC, COURT STAFF). (Entered: 07/23/2025)\n07/24/2025 75 SLG TEXT ORDER as to Seth Herrera: In light of the pending Motion to Suppress, the Status Conference on August 6, 2025, is VACATED and is rescheduled to August 15, 2025, at 10:00 a.m. in Anchorage\nCourtroom 2. (BJK, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 07/24/2025)\n07/24/2025 76 *** DISREGARD. SLG TEXT ORDER as to Matthew Etwand Coley: In light of the Discovery Management Conference on July 28, 2025, the Trial Scheduling Conference on August 1, 2025, is vacated and rescheduled\nto August 15, 2025, at 10:15 a.m. in Anchorage Courtroom 2. (BJK, COURT STAFF) Modified on 7/24/2025 to reflect error-Entered into incorrect case. Parties are advised to disregard. (BJK, COURT STAFF). (Entered:\n07/24/2025)\n07/28/2025 77 SLG TEXT ORDER as to Seth Herrera: The Government's Motion to Accept Over-Length Brief at Docket 71 and Motion for Leave to File Exhibit Under Seal at Docket 73 are each GRANTED. The Government's\nOpposition at Docket 70 is ACCEPTED AS FILED and the Government's Exhibit 1 at Docket 73-1 shall remain SEALED. (JDS, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 07/28/2025)\n07/29/2025 78 SLG TEXT ORDER as to Seth Herrera: Defendant's Motion for Leave to File Reply at Docket 74 is GRANTED. Defendant may file a reply to the Government's Opposition to Defendant's Motion to Suppress by July\n31, 2025. (JDS, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 07/29/2025)\n07/31/2025 79 SLG TEXT ORDER as to Seth Herrera: Due to the Court's trial schedule, the Status Conference on August 15, 2025, is VACATED and rescheduled to September 9, 2025, at 1:45 p.m. in Anchorage Courtroom 2.\n(LMH, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 07/31/2025)\n08/01/2025 80 SEALED NOTICE of Filing Reply by Seth Herrera re 78 Order,, Terminate Motions,, Set/Reset Motion and R&R Deadlines/Hearings, 70 Response in Opposition (Attachments: # 1 Reply to Govt's Opposition)(Muse,\nBen) (Entered: 08/01/2025)\n08/01/2025 81 MOTION to Seal Reply at Doc. 80 by Seth Herrera. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Order)(Muse, Ben) (Entered: 08/01/2025)\n08/01/2025 82 MOTION to Accept Late Filing re 80 Notice (Other) - SEALED pdf (Reply) by Seth Herrera. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Order)(Muse, Ben) (Entered: 08/01/2025)\n08/01/2025 83 SLG TEXT ORDER as to Seth Herrera: The Motion to Seal Reply at Docket 81 is GRANTED. The Reply at Docket 80 is SEALED. A redacted, public version of the Reply shall be available as soon as practicable after\nthe parties confer regarding redaction, and no later than August 15, 2025. (LMH, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 08/01/2025)\n08/01/2025 84 SLG TEXT ORDER as to Seth Herrera: The Motion to Accept Late Filing at Docket 82 is GRANTED. The Defendants Reply at Docket 80 is accepted as filed. (LMH, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 08/01/2025)\n08/08/2025 85 MOTION for Leave to File Surreply and for Oral Argument by USA as to Seth Herrera. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Order)(Rothberg, Rachel) (Entered: 08/08/2025)\n08/11/2025 86 RESPONSE in Opposition by Seth Herrera re 85 MOTION for Leave to File Surreply and for Oral Argument PARTIAL OPPOSITION (Muse, Ben) (Entered: 08/11/2025)\n08/13/2025 87 SLG TEXT ORDER: Due to the pending Motion to Suppress, the Status Conference on September 9, 2025, is VACATED and will be rescheduled in due course. (BJK, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 08/13/2025)\n08/20/2025 88 ORDER as to Seth Herrera: The MOTION for Leave to File Surreply and for Oral Argumentre 85 is GRANTED. Oral Argument re 54 is GRANTED. Oral Argument set for 9/16/2025 at 10:30 AM in Anchorage\nCourtroom 2 before Sharon L. Gleason. Signed by Judge Sharon L. Gleason on 8/19/25. (BJK, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 08/20/2025)\n08/21/2025 89 UNOPPOSED MOTION to Continue Oral Argument by USA as to Seth Herrera. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Order)(Rothberg, Rachel) (Entered: 08/21/2025)\n08/29/2025 90 SLG TEXT ORDER as to Seth Herrera: The Unopposed Motion to Continue Oral Argument at Docket 89 is GRANTED. Oral Argument on September 16, 2025, is VACATED and rescheduled to October 15, 2025, at\n11:00 a.m. in Anchorage Courtroom 2. The Court finds excludable delay through 10/15/2025 under 18 U.S.C. \u00a7 3161 (h)(1)(D), delay resulting from any pretrial motion, and 18 U.S.C. \u00a7 \u00a7 3161 (h)(7)(A); (h)(7)(B)(i) and\n(iv), the ends of justice served by taking such action outweigh the best interest of the public and the defendant in a speedy trial. (LMH, COURT STAFF) Modified on 8/29/2025 to correct date (LMH, COURT STAFF).\n(Entered: 08/29/2025)\n08/29/2025 ***Terminate Deadlines and Hearings as to Seth Herrera:, ***Set/Reset Deadlines re Motion or Report and Recommendation in case as to Seth Herrera 54 MOTION to Suppress Evidence. Motion Hearing set for\n10/15/2025 11:00 AM in Anchorage Courtroom 2 before Sharon L. Gleason. (LMH, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 08/29/2025)\n10/08/2025 91 SLG TEXT ORDER as to Seth Herrera: Due to a conflict in the Court's calendar, Oral Argument on October 15, 2025, is vacated and rescheduled to the same day at 3:00 p.m. in Anchorage Courtroom 2. (JDS, COURT\nSTAFF) (Entered: 10/08/2025)\n10/10/2025 92 SLG TEXT ORDER as to Seth Herrera: At the request of counsel, the time of Oral Argument on October 15, 2025, is AMENDED to the same day at 3:15 p.m. in Anchorage Courtroom 2. (JDS, COURT STAFF)\n(Entered: 10/10/2025)\n10/15/2025 93 MINUTE ENTRY for proceedings held before Chief District Judge Sharon L. Gleason: Oral Argument on Motion to Suppress Evidence 54 as to Seth Herrera held at 3:12 PM to 4:08 PM on 10/15/2025. Arguments heard.\nMatter taken UNDER ADVISEMENT, written ruling to issue. APPEARANCES: Defendant present, In-custody; Rachel Lieber Rothberg and Mac Caille Petursson, AUSA; Ben W. Muse, AFD; Stacy M. Baldwin, Official\nCourt Reporter. (SCD, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 10/15/2025)\n12/30/2025 TSC set for 1/27/2026 at 10:00 AM in Anchorage Courtroom 2 before Sharon L. Gleason. (BJK, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 12/30/2025)\n01/05/2026 95 UNOPPOSED MOTION to Appear Telephonically by USA as to Seth Herrera. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Order)(Rothberg, Rachel) (Entered: 01/05/2026)\n01/05/2026 96 NOTICE of Proposed Redactions by USA as to Seth Herrera re 94 Sealed Order,, Terminate Motions, (Attachments: # 1 Exhibit Proposed Redacted Version)(Rothberg, Rachel) (Entered: 01/05/2026)\n01/09/2026 97 SLG TEXT ORDER as to Seth Herrera: The Unopposed Motion to Appear Telephonically at Docket 95 is GRANTED. Trial Attorney Rachel L. Rothberg may appear telephonically at the Trial Scheduling Conference on\nJanuary 27, 2026 at 10:00 am, by dialing 571-353-2301 (Call ID 020262828, Pin 487051) approximately five minutes before the scheduled hearing time. (JDV, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 01/09/2026)\n01/20/2026 98 SLG TEXT ORDER as to Seth Herrera: This Court entered a sealed order at Docket 94 DENYING Defendant's Motion to Suppress at Docket 54 . A redacted and unsealed version of the Court's sealed order is available\nat Docket [96-1]. (JDS, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 01/20/2026)\n01/27/2026 99 MINUTE ENTRY for proceedings held before Chief Judge Sharon L. Gleason: Trial Scheduling Conference as to Seth Herrera held at 10:04 AM to 10:07 AM on 1/27/2026. Court and counsel heard re setting a trial date\nand pending case in Western District of Texas. Final Pretrial Conference set for 4/28/2026 at 2:00 PM and Trial by Jury set for 5/11/2026 at 8:30 AM in Anchorage Courtroom 2. Trial scheduling order to follow. The\nCourt found the ends of justice served by taking such action outweigh the best interest of the public and the defendant in a speedy trial and excluded time under 18 USC \u00a7\u00a7 3161 (h)(7)(A), (h)(7)(B)(i), and (h)(7)(B)(iv)\nthrough 5/11/2026. APPEARANCES: Defendant WAIVED, In-custody; Mac Caille Petursson and Rachel Rothberg (Tel), AUSA; Ben W. Muse, AFD; Stacy M. Baldwin, Official Court Reporter. (SCD, COURT STAFF)\n(Entered: 01/27/2026)\n01/29/2026 100 SECOND AMENDED CRIMINAL PRETRIAL AND TRIAL SCHEDULING ORDER: Final Pretrial Conference set for 4/28/2026 at 2:00 PM and Trial by Jury set for 5/11/2026 at 8:30 AM in Anchorage\nCourtroom 2. See Order for additional deadlines. Signed by Judge Sharon L. Gleason on 1/29/2026. (JDV, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 01/29/2026)\n02/17/2026 101 NOTICE OF EXPERT WITNESS UNDER FEDERAL RULE 16(a)(1)(G) by USA as to Seth Herrera (Rothberg, Rachel) (Entered: 02/17/2026)\n03/25/2026 102 MOTION to Continue Trial and All Trial-Related Deadlines (Non-Opposed) by Seth Herrera. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Order)(Muse, Ben) (Entered: 03/25/2026)\n03/30/2026 103 SLG TEXT ORDER as to Seth Herrera: Defendant's Non-Opposed Motion to Continue Trial and All Trial-Related Deadlines at Docket 102 is GRANTED. The Final Pretrial Conference on April 27, 2026, is VACATED\nand CONTINUED to August 4, 2026, at 1:00 p.m. in Anchorage Courtroom 2. The Trial by Jury set to begin on May 11, 2026, is VACATED and CONTINUED to August 17, 2026 in Anchorage Courtroom 2. The Court\nfinds the ends of justice served by taking such action outweigh the best interest of the public and the defendant in a speedy trial and excludes time under 18 USC \u00a7 3161 (h)(7)(A), (h)(7)(B)(i), and (h)(7)(B)(iv) from May\n11, 2026, to August 17, 2026. (ANM, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 03/30/2026)\n03/30/2026 104 THIRD AMENDED CRIMINAL PRETRIAL AND TRIAL SCHEDULING ORDER as to Seth Herrera: Dispositive Motions due by 5/26/2026. Final Pretrial Conference set for 8/4/2026 at 1:00 p.m. and the Trial by\nJury set for 8/17/2026 at 8:30 a.m. in Anchorage Courtroom 2 before Sharon L. Gleason. Signed by Judge Sharon L. Gleason on 3/30/2026. (ANM, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 03/30/2026)\n05/26/2026 105 NOTICE REGARDING EXPERT WITNESS UNDER FEDERAL RULE 16(a)(1)(G) by USA as to Seth Herrera re 101 Notice (Other) (Rothberg, Rachel) (Entered: 05/26/2026)\n06/09/2026 106 NOTICE OF INTENT TO CHANGE PLEA as to Seth Herrera (Muse, Ben) (Entered: 06/09/2026)\n06/11/2026 107 SLG TEXT ORDER as to Seth Herrera: In light of Defendant's Notice of Intent to Change Plea at Docket 106 , this matter is referred to Judge Kyle F. Reardon for a proposed Change of Plea hearing. The Final Pretrial\nConference on August 4, 2026, and the Trial by Jury set to begin on August 17, 2026, are hereby VACATED. (ANM, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 06/11/2026)\n06/12/2026 108 NOTICE of Consent to Transfer under Rule 20 for Plea and Sentence by USA as to Seth Herrera (Rothberg, Rachel) (Entered: 06/12/2026)\n\nPACER Service Center\nTransaction Receipt\n06/13/2026 18:05:40\nPACER\nmrinaal_ramachandran Client Code:\nLogin:\nSearch 3:24-cr-00091-\nDescription: Docket Report\nCriteria: SLG-KFR\nBillable\n10 Cost: 1.00\nPages:"
